WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.150
<i>October 5th. The 11th
year of the Bun'ei era...</i>

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.660
<i>The Mongol Navy appeared 
in Sasu Bay, Tsushima,</i>

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.020
<i>landing with a force of 
over 1,000 Goryeo soldiers.</i>

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.080
<i>The local ruler of Tsushima, Sou Sukekuni,</i>

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>had only 80 horses and 200 infantry.</i>

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:24.200
<i>Outnumbered, the Tsushima forces 
were routed after a fierce battle.</i>

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.080
Retreat! Retreat!

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.180
Fall back and regroup!

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:40.010
<i>Shit! "Regroup"?</i>

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.870
<i>We've lost both our lord and his son,</i>

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.810
<i>and our morale's as low as it can go.</i>

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.190
<i>This is a disaster!</i>

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.600
That armor...

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.180
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.400
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.740
Whoa, whoa...

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.110
Whoa, whoa...

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.880
Okay, you're all good horses.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.180
The exile!

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.630
That armor...

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.400
They're here!

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.690
Keep running!

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.930
Listen up, everyone!

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.050
The enemy is so eager to pursue you 
that they've overstretched their lines.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
Now is the time to strike.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.450
Listen up, everyone!

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.070
Turn around!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.990
We're about to charge 
right at the Mongol forces!

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:06.030
No one asked for your opinion, exile!

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.620
Do you even know what's happening here?

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.030
You suffered a pathetic defeat,

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.630
and now you're running, right?

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.720
But the Mongols are so eager 
to hunt you down that they've

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.000
stretched themselves into a thin 
line at the bottom of this valley.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.630
And now they've lost the general who was 
leading them and are falling out of order.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.390
Now's our chance to strike!

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:26.400
Ridiculous. If you want to go, go yourself!

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.560
What's wrong? Come get these horses!

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.350
Of course! It took a little 
time to get armored up.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.470
It just doesn't feel right 
wearing somebody else's.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.410
So I guess we fight, after all.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.450
Who are you?

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.270
"Who are we?"

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.140
We're the exiles you 
begged to come save you.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.060
It stinks!

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.690
All of you,

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:50.380
we won't lose like Sou Sukekuni did!

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:53.620
You're just bandits!

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.630
My name is Kuchii Jinzaburou!

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.080
Are you cowards?

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:01.660
How do you intend to see 
an end to this battle?

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.620
How do you intend to face tomorrow?

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:08.300
Are you such weaklings that you won't fight 
unless an outsider like me tells you to?

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.600
If you are, then run and 
hide from the Mongols,

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.920
and then crawl on the 
ground until you're dead!

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.820
What?!

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:15.970
You bastard...

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.640
You don't need inspiring words, do you?

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.120
Listen!

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.110
You're not following mere exiles!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.040
You're following this armor!

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.340
This armor, which you revere as
the treasure of the founder of the Sou Clan.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.330
Let's go!

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.050
Damn it!

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.270
Let's get going!

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.320
Follow him!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.980
There's only about 30 or 40 of them.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.920
About a third, I guess?

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.470
Not bad for the terrified 
soldiers of a defeated army.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.530
You know how to inspire a warrior.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:53.240
Make sure the ones 
who followed us stay alive!

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.260
I'll open the way for them!

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:08.610
Hey, is he a monster?

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.370
Oh, he's starting to get excited.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:16.240
I, Obusuma Saburou, was once known as  
the great general of the Musashi Province.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.620
<b>Obusuma Saburou</b>

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.660
I won't let a young brat like you outfight me!

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.190
Bows take too much time!

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:34.930
I, Shiraishi Kazuhisa, have no rivals 
when it comes to fighting on horseback!

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.640
<b>Shiraishi Kazuhisa</b>

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.150
<b>Hitari</b>

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:46.520
Don't let the exiles kill 
more Mongols than we do!

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.500
Have our vanguard fall back.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.410
We'll bring the Japanese into our ranks,

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.460
surround them from all 
directions and kill them!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.070
Yes, sir.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.620
Retreat!

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.070
There we go! The enemy's retreating!

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:05.930
Follow them!

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.440
They're trying to regroup?

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.970
It's a deliberate feint.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.180
Stop everyone from following, Kuchii-dono!

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.720
No, we have to pursue!

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.680
It's insane to chase them 
with these numbers!

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.280
The flow of battle means everything in war!

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.710
If they're confident they outnumber 
us and don't set their trap right,

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.610
we can turn the tables on them.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:29.560
Everyone, the battle is as good as won!

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:33.720
Follow right after me!

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:37.210
Look! The enemy is retreating!

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:39.050
We can't just sit here and watch!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.080
Wait, you idiots!

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.170
Abiru Yajirou-dono, shouldn't we stop them?

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:49.600
You're our lord's adopted son, 
you must take command.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.340
How can we face our fallen lord 
if we let the exiles take control?

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.100
Genpachi-dono.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.550
We failed to protect both 
our lord and his son.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.400
We have no choice.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:11.890
Foolishness...

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.530
That's just what happened today.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.750
We'll pursue too deep and be 
crushed by their numbers again.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:20.340
Abiru-dono!

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.310
What's wrong?

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:23.410
P-Princess Teruhi-sama..

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.370
What?

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.470
Kousuke... You fought so well out there...

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:29.950
Your words honor me.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.210
Princess Teruhi...

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.330
What are you doing here?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.840
Return to the capital!

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.300
It was your father's last command!

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.550
We have failed!

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:47.030
Our lord, his son, and most 
of the Sou Clan have been slain...

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:50.100
I've heard.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.690
I just passed by the soldiers 
who fled into the mountains

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.620
and heard what happened in the battle.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.020
I am the daughter of a samurai.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.940
I was prepared for this.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:03.530
That's why I came.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:04.890
I know how to use a bow, at least.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:06.190
No.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:09.280
We can't let you stay here.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.810
Gontarou, take her home.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.060
Silence, Abiru-dono.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:16.550
Listen, everyone!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.310
I, Teruhi, will now take 
command in my father's place!

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.060
Reporting in!

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:26.820
Our allies that charged the 
enemy have been surrounded,

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.620
and we can no longer see them!

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.000
They were wiped out?

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.610
I should've, at least, stopped the ones 
who tried to follow the exiles...

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.540
Exiles?

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:39.950
Is Kuchii Jinzaburou on the battlefield now?

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.110
<i>Now that we've leapt into the flame,</i>

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:44.400
<i>there's no going back!</i>

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:50.240
<i>It's been a long time 
since I've felt this...</i>

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.000
<i>My stomach's twisting itself into knots!</i>

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.070
<i>That's their headquarters?</i>

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:56.480
<i>And that's...</i>

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:58.410
That single point, there!

00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.550
Let's go!

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.040
Surround them!

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:33.630
The local lord's holding out 
longer than I expected.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:37.000
You're not going to tell us 
we're going down there, right?

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.790
I don't know.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:43.240
The emperor is the one 
who makes all the decisions.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.110
They're here!

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.070
Our allies have returned!

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.210
They broke through the encirclement?

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:56.620
Are there Mukuri pursuers?

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:57.760
No!

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.190
The Mukuri ranks seem to be in chaos...

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.740
<i>Is that Jinzaburou?</i>

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:17.970
What? You cut your way into their headquarters
and slew their general and his men?

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:18.770
Yes.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:22.290
The exiles were amazing.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.130
With so few soldiers?

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.110
Unbelievable.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.630
We can't believe it ourselves.

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.510
This would've been impossible 
without Kuchii-dono.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:39.820
I need you to confirm that 
these are what I think they are.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.900
The Mukuri general?

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:42.980
No.

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.150
This is...

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:49.180
Sou Sukekuni and Umajirou-dono.

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:54.390
Princess!

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.220
I had to take some risks to get these,

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.210
and some of the men paid 
with their lives, but it was necessary.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:04.250
If these heads were hanging from 
the enemy's spears tomorrow,

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:05.960
it would damage our morale.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.120
My lord... My young master...

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.480
How sad!

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:20.250
You died for the pride of 
Tsushima and the Sou Clan!

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:23.620
Sou Sukekuni lost.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.250
That's why he died.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:27.330
That's all there is to it.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.570
What?

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:31.460
He fought with all his 
strength to win the victory,

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.570
and then he failed and died.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:36.700
It was a proud death,

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:39.350
but he did not die for pride.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:49.470
Father... Brother!

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.650
There they are.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:10.970
I can see 'em clearly.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:15.510
Don't underestimate my night vision.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.500
<b>Amushi</b>

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.230
<i>Father, Brother...</i>

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:25.650
<i>Please forgive me for having nothing more 
than these river stones to offer you now.</i>

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:31.150
Everyone, prepare to cross the mountains.

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:33.200
We're getting back 
to the capital by morning.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.050
Yes, sir.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:36.100
Where are the exiles?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.750
They went to the cave behind the shrine.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.470
They said they needed to rest.

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:42.110
Selfish, uncaring bastards...

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:55.870
Why did you come back now?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.530
We were together most of the way.

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:01.760
Where did you run off to?

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:05.380
You were the ones who left me behind 
while I was taking a shit.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:09.190
Any idiot could tell you a pirate 
is going to get lost in the mountains.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:12.270
It doesn't matter. Just don't 
take up too much space.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.320
This was once a silver mine.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.800
It's pretty handy.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:22.190
Its opening doesn't face the sea, so the 
enemy can't see the smoke from our fires.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:25.570
But that will only save us 
for tonight, Kuchii-dono.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:29.070
If we stay here, the Mongols 
will kill us all on the morn.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:34.950
I've got two wives and seven 
children back in Kyushu.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.970
And I keep thinking of them 
when I see the slain...

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:42.610
Do you have a wife or child in Kamakura?

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:44.760
A wife?

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.110
The most I ever had was four.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.880
If you're not careful, you find yourself with

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.620
more and and more marriages from your 
relatives and the place you grew up in.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:55.800
But, in the end, I just got tired of it.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.180
Only one remained,

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:02.630
along with one daughter.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.150
<i>It's been four years since then, huh?</i>

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:10.040
My wife and child are gone.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.240
They both died in a plague.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.680
I was gone to war for a month,

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:17.900
and when I came back, they were buried.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:21.470
It's not like slitting an 
enemy's throat open in a war.

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:24.260
They don't really feel dead to me.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:25.830
I see.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.490
Princess.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:30.170
I brought them as you asked.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:31.760
I-I see.

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:38.670
Villagers of Sasu, I am Teruhi, 
daughter of your lord.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:41.810
It's not much, but we've come 
to bring you some dried rice.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.310
Princess Teruhi!

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:48.990
You once came here with 
our lord and his son, yes?

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.140
It's been many years, elder.

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:52.960
But I appreciate the kindness 
you showed me then.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:55.860
There's something I need to tell you all.

00:14:56.510 --> 00:15:01.030
I want you to head to 
the capital with us tonight.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:04.340
We've lost two-thirds of our forces,

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.130
and this valley is doomed.

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:08.770
I'm sure you may be reluctant to do so,

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.880
but will you come with us?

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:15.650
I'm going to sleep.

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.240
Wake me up when the moon is high in the sky.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:19.600
You're going to sleep?

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.360
We need to head to the capital 
as soon as possible.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:23.760
We're not going to the capital.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.650
Once I wake up, we're doing 
a night raid on the Mongols.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:29.860
A night raid?

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.360
Are you insane?

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.070
Villagers of Sasu,

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:35.790
can one of you guide me?

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:36.970
Wait.

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:39.450
Everyone's exhausted 
from this afternoon's battle!

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.700
What?

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.780
You want me to fight your war, right?

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:45.380
Not to get yourself killed!

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:49.230
We need to retreat 
to the capital and regroup.

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:51.660
And then we can come up with a plan...

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.480
I won't force anybody.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:54.900
Make your own choice.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.130
But if a smaller force 
wants to beat a larger one,

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.800
it has to hit them in their sleep.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:03.450
They're a long way from home, 
in a place they've never been,

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.350
and it's the thing that terrifies them most.

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:10.600
Show them that a cornered 
rat can kill a cat, too!

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:14.290
What a pain.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:18.040
General, let me be your guide.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.150
No, not just a guide...

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:22.260
Let me join the attack.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:25.630
I've always been the strongest 
warrior in my village.

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.680
But I...

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:29.770
I couldn't protect my wife and children.

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:33.880
They were taken from me by the Mukuri!

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:36.930
Ginshichi, I'm going, too.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.030
My daughter was kidnapped.

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:40.780
I lost my son, too!

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:41.510
Let's go!

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.900
Rokurou! Shioya!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.690
Eat something.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.140
Yes, sir!

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:51.480
Yajirou-dono, is it okay to ignore this?

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:54.750
I don't care.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.980
We're going back to the capital.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:15.080
<i>I don't know how he can sleep 
so peacefully in this situation.</i>

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:17.480
<i>What kind of warrior is he?</i>

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:19.780
<i>A night ambush?</i>

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:23.100
<i>All he needs to do is defend us...</i>

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.570
<i>Kuchii Jinzaburou, you're dangerous.</i>

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.640
<i>Once the war begins,</i>

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:33.490
<i>you'll drag everyone 
to the pits of hell with you.</i>

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:38.760
<i>Maybe I should just kill you here...</i>

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:45.960
<i>I never should have summoned you here.</i>

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.320
What? Is the moon at its peak yet?

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:08.620
Yes.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:11.510
As we agreed,

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:15.650
we're wearing light armor, and we
covered up anything that can reflect light.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:20.690
Between the samurai, their followers, 
and the villagers from the valley,

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:22.730
there's 64 of us in all.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:28.500
But Abiru Yajirou and the rest of the Sou Clan's 
retainers have already fled towards the capital.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:35.280
You guys must be nuts 
to still be here, then.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.220
Aw, don't say that.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.160
You're the one who put us up to this.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:41.890
You were at the fight this afternoon, right?

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.630
Are you a soldier of the Sou Clan?

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.860
What's your name?

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:47.410
Oh, we've met?

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.740
Sasa Rantarou. Call me Sasara.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:51.180
Sasara, huh?

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:52.420
What's your name?

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:53.340
Hishiroku.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.530
Echizen Gorou Harutada.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:57.360
I am Yaguruma, his follower.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.060
Did Obusuma Saburou run?

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.910
I don't like fighting on land.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.030
What are you making?

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:08.540
<b>Douen</b>

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.530
I'll see you off here.

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:09.780
I'm Koorogi.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:11.010
Aosuke.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:12.830
Is that all?

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:16.850
The only ones left are our guides, 
Ginshichi, Rokurou, and Shioya.

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.050
And Teruhi.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.810
I shall accompany you as your strategist.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:24.100
You have no complaints, right?

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.110
Princess, reconsider this.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:27.090
Shut up.

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:29.210
Whatever.

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.000
Let's go.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.820
Go? Um?

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.350
We're attacking?

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:34.180
Yeah.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:37.250
I thought you were going to take a piss.

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:40.700
Amushi?

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:41.760
Yeah.

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:43.800
I took a look for you.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:45.400
You were right.

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:49.140
Most of the Mongols went back 
on their ships to sleep.

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:52.630
Only half the ones from this 
afternoon are still on the beach.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.870
I knew it. Thanks.

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:56.680
You're going to pay me for this, right?

00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:00.150
Yeah. I'll go snatch something for you.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:05.680
<i>Well, I already got something for myself.</i>

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.440
<i>Mongol treasure.</i>

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.070
<i>I can't wait to see what's inside.</i>

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:17.510
We ride into the enemy camp, set fire to it, 
stir up a fuss, and then immediately get out.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.140
This ambush will protect us in the future.

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:22.500
Protect us?

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:26.300
If the enemy knows they 
can be attacked, they'll be careful.

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:30.570
And that will make them a little slower.

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.960
We can buy a little extra time,

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:37.040
which we can use to get 
as far away as possible.

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:39.640
The Mongols are after Kyushu.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.050
They won't want to spend 
months on this island.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.970
So we hide deep in the island,

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.800
where they can't reach us.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.130
The wounded, the women, the children,

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.650
and us, too.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.160
Everyone, fight hard!

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:00.960
Our deaths tonight will help 
Tsushima survive tomorrow!

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:08.720
There's still 200 steps 
or so to the main camp.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:12.620
It doesn't look like there's 
any place to hide here.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:15.380
Can we get to 50 steps away, Ginshichi?

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.380
If we head into the low ground 
where there's no light

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.000
and then approach from the right, maybe.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.680
Then that watchman...

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:24.740
We'll have to wait for him to go.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.510
Off he goes.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:30.390
Yeah, that was faster than I thought.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.210
Karudoraga!

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:34.550
Karudoraga!

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:36.510
Karudoraga! Karudoraga!

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:36.510
What are they doing?

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:39.480
Karudoraga! Karudoraga!

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:43.480
Wait.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:46.980
They betrayed us?!

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:50.090
My love...

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:50.750
Daddy!

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:53.990
He's...

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:57.920
Over here!

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
<b>Episode 3:
Time To Strike</b>
